{#
The unread count on a category tab, and a way into that tab's unread mail (#670).

The sidebar's unread badges have been links to their row's unread view for a
while; the same round pill on a tab looked the same and did nothing of its own,
so a click on "Updates 3" opened all of Updates and the three were still a
toolbar click away. Now it opens them, and answers the pointer and the keyboard
the way the sidebar's does.

A SIBLING of the tab's own link, never inside it — an <a> inside an <a> is not
markup a browser keeps, the reason the sidebar's rows are a .nav-item wrapping
their anchor (see unread_badge() in _sidebar.html.twig). On the strips the tab
link is stretched over the whole tab with an ::after, so a click anywhere else
on the tab still opens the tab as it did, and this sits above that layer with
`relative z-10`.

  count  the number, rendered at zero too and hidden there, so the sidebar
         controller can patch it after a sync.
  href   the tab with `unread=1`.
  key    the counts endpoint's key, when the number is one it emits. The
         unified inbox's are; an account's own strip has no key, because the
         endpoint's per-tab numbers are summed across every account and would
         overwrite this one's with the wrong figure (see account.html.twig).

`data-tab-unread` is what the Tab counts setting hides by (app.css), and what
ui--sidebar patches by; the label template travels with it for that patcher.
Replaces the history entry, as a tab switch does: it IS a tab switch, with the
unread filter on.
#}
{% macro tab_unread_count(count, href, key = null) %}
    <a href="{{ href }}"
       data-turbo-frame="inbox-list-frame"
       data-turbo-action="replace"
       class="relative z-10 ml-1.5 text-xs font-semibold px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full shrink-0 bg-accent text-accent-ink
              transition-opacity hover:opacity-80
              focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent{{ count > 0 ? '' : ' hidden' }}"
       data-tab-unread
       {% if key is not null %}data-count-key="{{ key }}"{% endif %}
       data-label-template="{{ 'sidebar.badge.unread'|trans }}"
       aria-label="{{ 'sidebar.badge.unread'|trans({ '%count%': count }) }}"
    >{{ count }}</a>
{% endmacro %}

{#
The classes that stretch a tab's own link over the whole tab, so the tab stays
one big target with the count link above it. The focus ring is drawn on the
stretched layer, so tabbing to a tab outlines the tab and not just its name.
The tab box itself must be `relative`.
#}
{% macro tab_link_classes() %}after:absolute after:inset-0 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:after:ring-2 focus-visible:after:ring-inset focus-visible:after:ring-accent{% endmacro %}
